on getting into mechinterp:
Quoting @NeelNanda5
@jeremyphoward I find it hard to convert this into advice to give junior researchers. Like, in my incredibly biased opinion, it's a beautiful, fascinating, and really important field. I think it's also less neglected than some other very important fields esp within safety, but also way more neglected than the vast majority of ML. And the required thinking style is sufficiently different that some people who would be brilliant at mech interp won't be brilliant at most other fields and vice versa. My general advice to people trying to get into safety is that if they're indifferent between mech interp and something else, or feel obliged to do mech interp because it's the "cool thing", maybe they should try something else. But if they're excited about it, then fucking go for it

